* ASTRAN Technology Rules: GlobalFoundries gf180mcuD, 6 V devices of gf180mcu_fd_sc_mcu7t5v0
* (hand-written, see pdks/gf180/README.md; values are the *_MV rules of the klayout DRC decks)
* Astran layer -> gf180 layer: CONT = contact, MET1 = metal1, VIA1 = via1, MET2 = metal2, VIA2 = via2, MET3 = metal3.
* Where gf180 has several conditional rules for one Astran rule, the conservative value is used.
* Rule names are those of libs.tech/klayout/drc/rule_decks/*.drc.

TECHNAME	gf180mcuD
MINSTEP		0.005
MLAYERS		3

S1P1P1	0.24	* PL.3a
S2P1P1	0.24	* PL.3a
S2P1P1_1	0
S2P1P1_2	0
S3P1P1	0.24	* PL.3a
S1DFP1	0.3	* PL.5b_MV: field poly to related COMP
S2DFP1	0.3	* PL.5b_MV
S3DFP1	0
E1P1DF	0.22	* PL.4
E2P1DF	0.22	* PL.4
E1DFP1	0.4	* DF.6_MV: source/drain extension beyond gate
E1DNP1	0
E1DDP1	0
R1P1	0
S1DFP2	0
S1P1P2	0
W2CT	0.22	* CO.1
E1M1CT	0.005	* CO.6
E2M1CT	0.06	* CO.6a
E3M1CT	0.06	* CO.6a
E1DFCT	0.07	* CO.4
E2DFCT	0.07	* CO.4
E1P1CT	0.07	* CO.3
E2P1CT	0.07	* CO.3
E3P1CT	0.07	* CO.3
E1P2CT	0
S1CTP1	0.15	* CO.7: COMP contact to poly on COMP
S1CTDP	0
S1CTDN	0
S1CTDF	0.17	* CO.8: poly contact to COMP
S1CTP2	0
R1M1	0
R2M1	0
W2VI	0.26	* V1.1
E1M1VI	0.06	* V1.3d, conservative
E2M1VI	0.06	* V1.3d, conservative
E1M2VI	0.06	* V1.4c, conservative
S1M2M2	0.28	* M2.2a
S1M2M1	0
S1M1M2	0
R2M2	0
W2P1	0.2	* PL.1_MV: minimum poly width (gate lengths come from the netlist)
W2DF	0.3	* DF.1a_MV
W2V2	0.26	* V2.1
S1M1M1	0.23	* M1.2a
S2M1M1	0.23	* M1.2a
S3M1M1	0.23	* M1.2a
E1M2V2	0.06	* V2.x, conservative
S1CTCT	0.25	* CO.2a
S2CTCT	0.25	* CO.2a
S3CTCT	0.25	* CO.2a
E1INDF	0.1	* tap implant enclosure (Astran uses it for the tap strips; NP.5a's 0.23 around gates comes from pnselborder)
E1IPDF	0.1	* tap implant enclosure (see E1INDF)
E1WNDP	0.6	* DF.4c_MV: nwell overlap of PCOMP
S1DNWN	0.6	* conservative: mirrors DF.4c_MV
S2M2M2	0.3	* M2.2b wide metal
A1M1	0.145	* M1.3: 0.1444, rounded up to the 0.005 step
W1M1	0.23	* M1.1
W1M2	0.28	* M2.1
W1M3	0.28	* M3.1, same as metal2
W1M4	0
